  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental funds only (no enterprise funds). Statement p4 (Total Governmental Funds column) used for receipts/disbursements. Taxes 829,860 split into property 786,805 and motor vehicle 43,055 using the statement of activities general receipts (p2; sum ties). The 'Local' line (132,925) split into charges for services 56,839, interest income 73,118 (category Interest Income, attempt 2) and miscellaneous 2,968 using the statement of activities (p2; sum ties exactly), the same way as Taxes. Sale of surplus 3,758 in other_financing; transfers in/out 30,180 each (Road to Inheritance Tax). Ending cash = total fund balances 2,106,690 (cash 1,868,390 + restricted cash 238,300). Balance sheet (attempt 2): Statement of Assets and Fund Balances - Cash Basis, Governmental Funds (p3, Total Governmental Funds column, fund balance by classification), whose totals equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1, 2,106,690). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) used for General Fund column; its actuals differ slightly from the statement (receipts 738,124 vs 735,373 General Fund column, because of GASB 54 inheritance/reclassification note p10), and its department groupings differ from the statement's function columns (capital outlay is inside departments). The p5 General Fund column duplicates the budget schedule so only the Inheritance Tax Fund column was recorded. Nonmajor funds (8 columns, pp6-7) recorded as combined total column. Road fund budget actual receipts 783,052 vs statement 782,045 (1,007 sale of surplus shown separately in statement). Budget schedule lines with 0 actuals (transfers) omitted. Intergovernmental lines are not broken down anywhere in the report, so no homestead/property tax credit split is possible. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
